== phase geography per class (B-K condensation boundary M ~ 1e12/h; 1507.01019 eq 18 context) ==
  early: med logM_h=12.36; frac above condensation boundary (logM>12.15): 68%; med R_T=94 kpc vs med r200=241 kpc -> core/halo radius fraction 0.39
  late: med logM_h=11.86; frac above condensation boundary (logM>12.15): 27%; med R_T=79 kpc vs med r200=167 kpc -> core/halo radius fraction 0.48
  -> early-type halos sit at/above the condensation boundary far more often than late: less coherent
     superfluid (smaller phonon boost for their KINEMATICS), more normal-phase real mass. On the LENSING
     axis (this measurement) the offset is carried by the halo mass at fixed g_bar; the phase fork's
     DISTINCTIVE signature is kinematic-vs-lensing inconsistency per class, not the lensing split alone.

== verdict inputs (prereg T4 fork) ==
  sign: predicted + (early above) in ALL configs and ALL bins -> MATCHES the measured direction
  magnitude: type-blind +0.119 dex; +type-dep +0.401 dex vs measured +0.261 (u-r) / +0.185 (Sersic)
  ratios to u-r measurement: 0.46x (type-blind) .. 1.54x (type-dep)
  caveats carried: (i) 1-halo NFW only -- absolute g underpredicted at R>r200 (2-halo), but the split is
  the target and the low-g_bar bins are flagged; (ii) this is the generic CDM-envelope SHMR effect -- the
  locked wording applies: consistency for the real-lensing-mass CLASS, not 'SfDM confirmed' (Brouwer's own
  MICE/BAHAMAS sims disagree on the split); (iii) the same model FAILS the absolute lensing RAR shape
  (arXiv:2303.08560: chi2_red 15-29 vs parameter-free MOND 6.5 on the same data).
